From 627dec687fab5f62c518f41381e3b79a5963e5b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:08:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: RPC execution time by method

How long each RPC command takes to execute (CRPCTable::execute,
including commands that throw), by method. The label values are the
commands registered when metrics start, plus "other"; a method's series
appears once it has been called, so the exposition does not list a
hundred empty histograms.

(cherry picked from commit c4b2f4ff47d34184169112f6728a477322ee0d13)

N3-Source-Commit: c4b2f4ff47d34184169112f6728a477322ee0d13
N3-Source-Export: 0012

Metrics-Repair: Fold 18218fc4011c50e6628e7bbc89ec4c127bb1f26e at
this first per-method RPC duration owner. Canonical Beast dispatch calls
executeAsync, so timing only CRPCTable::execute missed HTTP requests. A
shared scope timer records both entry points, retains coroutine suspension
time and exception exits, and avoids duplicate instrumentation. The
original composed205 metrics functional failed its getblockcount count;
the scoped repair passed exact +1 native-async/sync-wrapper/error/wait
counts and at-least75ms duration for a100ms wait. The repaired source also
passed the four-target build,84 focused core+2T1 cases and4 standard
functionals. Those receipts belong to original source18218fc, not the
later composed209 endpoint; final standard gates remain required.
